@module flutter-m16 | Testing and Debugging
@summary Unit, widget and integration tests, mocking, DevTools, debugging and profiling.

@lesson flutter-m16-l01 | Unit testing | 8
## Learning objectives
- Test pure Dart logic

## Unit testing
Unit tests check functions and classes in isolation with `flutter_test`/`test`. They are fast and should cover your business logic.

```dart
import 'package:flutter_test/flutter_test.dart';

int add(int a, int b) => a + b;

void main() {
  test('adds numbers', () => expect(add(2, 3), 5));
}
```

## Summary
- Most tests should be fast unit tests.

@lesson flutter-m16-l02 | Widget testing | 8
## Learning objectives
- Test widgets without a device

## Widget testing
`testWidgets` pumps a widget in a test environment; find widgets with `find` and interact with `tester.tap`.

```dart
import 'package:flutter/material.dart';
import 'package:flutter_test/flutter_test.dart';

void main() {
  testWidgets('shows greeting', (tester) async {
    await tester.pumpWidget(const MaterialApp(home: Text('Hello')));
    expect(find.text('Hello'), findsOneWidget);
  });
}
```

## Summary
- pumpWidget, find, tap, pump.

@lesson flutter-m16-l03 | Integration testing | 8
## Learning objectives
- Test full flows on a device

## Integration testing
The `integration_test` package runs your real app on a device or emulator and drives it like a user.

```dart
import 'package:flutter_test/flutter_test.dart';
import 'package:integration_test/integration_test.dart';

void main() {
  IntegrationTestWidgetsFlutterBinding.ensureInitialized();
  testWidgets('app starts', (tester) async {
    // await tester.pumpWidget(const MyApp());
  });
}
```

## Summary
- Run with flutter test integration_test.

@lesson flutter-m16-l04 | Mocking | 8
## Learning objectives
- Replace dependencies with fakes and mocks

## Mocking
Use fakes or `mocktail` mocks to control dependencies such as APIs and clocks.

```dart
import 'package:mocktail/mocktail.dart';

abstract class Api { Future<String> name(); }
class MockApi extends Mock implements Api {}

void setup() {
  final api = MockApi();
  when(() => api.name()).thenAnswer((_) async => 'Ada');
}
```

## Summary
- Mock only what you don't own or can't control.

@lesson flutter-m16-l05 | Flutter DevTools | 8
## Learning objectives
- Inspect widgets, performance and memory

## Flutter DevTools
DevTools offers the Inspector, Performance view (frame timings), CPU profiler, Memory view and Network view. Open it from your IDE while the app runs.

```dart
// flutter run, then press 'v' or use your IDE's Open DevTools command
void main() {}
```

## Summary
- Use the right DevTools tab for each problem.

@lesson flutter-m16-l06 | Debugging | 8
## Learning objectives
- Find bugs with breakpoints and logging

## Debugging
Use breakpoints, step through code, inspect variables, and `debugPrint` for logs. Read the full stack trace: the first frame from your code is usually the culprit.

```dart
import 'package:flutter/foundation.dart';

void log(Object o) { if (kDebugMode) debugPrint('[bimo] $o'); }
```

## Summary
- Read stack traces from your own frames.

@lesson flutter-m16-l07 | Performance profiling | 8
## Learning objectives
- Measure jank in profile mode

## Performance profiling
Profile in `--profile` mode on a real device. Look for frames over 16 ms in the Performance view and use the CPU profiler to find hot spots.

```dart
// flutter run --profile
void main() {}
```

## Summary
- Never profile in debug mode.

@lesson flutter-m16-l08 | Memory leak prevention | 8
## Learning objectives
- Avoid leaks in Flutter apps

## Memory leak prevention
Dispose controllers, cancel subscriptions and timers, and avoid holding BuildContext or State in long-lived objects. Use DevTools Memory to verify.

```dart
import 'dart:async';

class Poller { Timer? t; void start() => t = Timer.periodic(const Duration(seconds: 5), (_) {}); void dispose() => t?.cancel(); }
```

## Summary
- Every listener needs a matching cancel.

@lesson flutter-m16-l09 | Error reporting | 8
## Learning objectives
- Capture errors from users

## Error reporting
Set `FlutterError.onError` and `PlatformDispatcher.instance.onError` to send errors to a service such as Crashlytics or Sentry.

```dart
import 'package:flutter/foundation.dart';
import 'package:flutter/material.dart';

void setup() {
  FlutterError.onError = (d) => debugPrint('report: ${d.exception}');
  PlatformDispatcher.instance.onError = (e, s) { debugPrint('report: $e'); return true; };
}
```

## Summary
- Report both framework and async errors.
